ts, ACLs, original data, and access behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-95ed851900884c53","cmd-edb87a6b25c04f5b","cmd-1e8c456c6ea94592","cmd-16f161e0f5b74ee9","cmd-b032fca1549c4d84","cmd-bd9b97999c9a43a1","cmd-eb9aea4e05e944c3","cmd-cf6506b071f543d9","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct configuration, functional, final-state, and post-restart evidence. The ACL design supports continuing nested inheritance, preserves designer ownership, grants reviewer effective read/write access, and denies visitor access. Existing content and the RHEL 9.8 platform were preserved. The mandatory node-restart protocol was fully demonstrated and cross-checked by lifecycle observations.","limitations":[]}
